00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Don't build in that place.

00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: Let's go to another verse.

00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:26.000
Boy, Satan is having fun with the disbelievers.

00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:29.000
Number 31 says,

00:55:29.000 --> 00:55:35.000
[30:31] You shall submit to GOD, reverence Him, observe the Contact Prayers (Salat), and do not be among the idol worshipers.

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:41.000
[30:32] Do not be among those who divide their religion into sects; each party rejoicing with what they have.

00:55:43.000 --> 00:55:48.000
We had a fellow come from the Sunni mosque here.

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:52.000
And he told Edip he's getting sick and tired of all the fighting that's going on there.

00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:58.000
Ok. I mean, here we are, we're reading the Quran, we all agree on a certain principle in here.

00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:00.000
But over there, they have different sects.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:06.000
And if you, if you favor one sect and not the other one, they have fights.

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: What did he tell you?

00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:13.000
Edip: All he said was "I have (unintelligible). They hate each other there. It's not (unintelligible)."

00:56:13.000 --> 00:56:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's always like that.

00:56:17.000 --> 00:56:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because they do not follow this commandment.

00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:25.000
[30:32] Do not be among those who divide their religion into sects; each party rejoicing with what they have.

00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:31.000
See, if you looked at us 15 years ago, this fellow would be my enemy. I'll be his enemy. Because he'll be a Shia, I'll be a Sunni.

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:39.000
And this will be... But look, now we're sitting one, united, loving each other.

00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:48.000
A man: Rashad, even among the Shias, I don't know if you know or not, but (unintelligible) it's like when they do the Namaz.

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:55.000
A man: The person who leads the Namaz doesn't mean that he is the most knowledgeable or not.

00:56:55.000 --> 00:57:04.000
A man: Everybody... But in Shia, you go to Imam Reza, for instance, such and such Imam or whatever,

00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:08.000
A man: and there are different groups. And they just know he is better or so you...

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, this is also true with the Sunnis.

00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. A man: Because of... So, you see several groups.

00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:19.000
A man: They are doing it at the same time, but some people go behind people, some people go right side, and one more (unintelligible) religion.

00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, it has to be the oldest man and the most knowledgeable.

00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:27.000
And I remember we had a 90-year-old man that was a Mullah.

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:32.000
I used to pray Fajr in the patron saint of my hometown, in the mosque.

00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:34.000
And quite often we'll go wake him up from Sujud.

00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:36.000
We'll make him Sujud.

00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:42.000
He never, he never gets up, you know.

00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:46.000
We used to say "Hey, Mawlana."

00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:55.000
And literally...Wait, wait a minute. When he died, I swear, when he died, President Sadat made a tomb for him.

00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:58.000
And people go now and they worship at his tomb, this particular man.

00:57:59.000 --> 00:58:00.000
His name was Sheikh Hijab.

00:58:01.000 --> 00:58:06.000
Boy, I dreaded every time I go and saw him because it took one hour to pray Fajr.

00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:11.000
Half of them Sujud. No, three quarters Sujud.

00:58:15.000 --> 00:58:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah. Really. Yes.

00:58:18.000 --> 00:58:20.000
He was very, very old.

00:58:20.000 --> 00:58:22.000
It has to be... There's a system in Sunnis.

00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:28.000
I guess Abdul Hayy thought that since we do it here, this way, we all take turns. It doesn't matter who's leading.

00:58:28.000 --> 00:58:30.000
This is the Sunni system. It is not.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:33.000
The Sunni system and apparently also the Shia system,

00:58:33.000 --> 00:58:36.000
there is priorities for leading the prayer.

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:38.000
A man: One of them is (unintelligible) handicapped.

00:58:39.000 --> 00:58:41.000
Dr. Khalifa: Should not be handicapped? A man: Handicapped.

00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: I wish I knew that then.

00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:44.000
A man: Tunnels Beach.

00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:46.000
A man: Tunnels Beach.

00:58:50.000 --> 00:58:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Capistrano Beach?

00:59:04.000 --> 00:59:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, faster.

00:59:13.000 --> 00:59:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: They have to ask, they have to ask you "are you a bastard?"

00:59:20.000 --> 00:59:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: I'm sure these are written in a book, as to the priorities, the conditions of leading the Prayer.

00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: What else?

00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:31.000
A man: Edip, what about if they're all bastards?

00:59:31.000 --> 00:59:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: I know they have to be, it has to be the oldest one and most knowledgeable, and so on. There's a set of priorities.

00:59:39.000 --> 00:59:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: Huh?

00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Yes.

00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: They do. Actually, they say "I am more worthy of leading a Prayer than you. I have a PhD from the Azhar University."

00:59:48.000 --> 00:59:53.000
And the other will say "I have the PhD plus this and that. I'm also seven days older than you."

00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:55.000
Really.

00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:57.000
Yes.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:03.000
A man: Humbly.

01:00:03.000 --> 01:00:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

01:00:05.000 --> 01:00:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: The Ahmadi Mullah in Canada said "I will humbly lead the prayer." Ismail Barakat said "you will humbly sit down right there."

01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:17.000
He said it, he said it very angrily.

01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:27.000
He's supposed to be here, by the way.

01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:30.000
Ismail, Ismail Barakat.

01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Saeed Talari will be here on Thursday, IN SHAA ALLAH.

01:00:34.000 --> 01:00:35.000
A man: IN SHAA ALLAH.

